Hammurabi — credits and provenance

Original game
-------------

"Hammurabi" (also known as "Sumeria" or "The Sumer Game") was written by Doug
Dyment in 1968 in FOCAL and was popularised, in BASIC and under the name
HAMURABI, by David H. Ahl in *101 BASIC Computer Games* (Creative Computing,
Morristown, New Jersey, 1978). The documented behaviour of the 1978 listing is
the rules reference for this project; see docs/plan.md section 4.

This repository
---------------

This repository is an independent Python re-implementation by kilofkilofa. It
contains no code from the original listings: the rules are re-implemented from
their documented behaviour rather than translated line by line, and the wording
of the reports belongs to this port. The lines that do survive verbatim - the
title HAMURABI and the "CREATIVE COMPUTING  MORRISTOWN, NEW JERSEY" subtitle in
src/hammurabi/ui.py - are kept as a nod to the original and are a title and a
short phrase, not a protected passage.

